 "verdict": "NEGATIVE: per-question ADAPTIVE bandit allocation does NOT beat fixed uniform pooling for oracle@B (best pooled held-out bandit \u0394=+0.002 over B in [2, 4, 8]; Thompson/UCB-E track uniform, sometimes losing to exploration cost) -- just like Markowitz (\u0394=+0.020). WHY: the optimistic in-sample clairvoyant ceiling suggests per-question structure (\u0394=+0.104), but it double-dips on the same 8 samples; the DE-BIASED split-oracle ceiling (perfect but finite FREE correctness signal, arm chosen on an independent half) shrinks to \u0394=+0.052 and INVERTS at B=8 (\u0394=-0.026) because single-arm concentration cannot match uniform's cross-arm coverage. So the reachable headroom is small AND the verifier score is too weak to capture it: fixed uniform pooling is already near-optimal for oracle@B (mirrors the Markowitz finding; consistent with the selection wall)."
}